---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import "../../styles/discover.css";
import "../../styles/reader.css";

// The advertising terms (DESIGN §11.10, §12): what buyers of placements and Author Pro agree to.
// Plain language; the rules here are the ones the code applies.
const UPDATED = "2026-09-27";
---

<Base title="Advertising terms" description="The rules for promotions and Author Pro on ReadLitRPG: what we accept, payment, cancellations, refunds and reporting." canonical="/legal/advertising">
  <div class="prose">
    <h1>Advertising terms</h1>
    <p class="muted">Last updated {UPDATED}.</p>

    <h2>Who can advertise</h2>
    <p>
      Authors who manage a profile on ReadLitRPG, for books listed on that profile. Only a profile's owners can pay. A restricted
      profile can't buy promotions.
    </p>

    <h2>What we accept</h2>
    <p>Ads for in-scope books in our catalog (LitRPG, progression fantasy, GameLit, cultivation and close relatives). We don't accept:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>books outside that scope, or books with plagiarism or rights disputes;</li>
      <li>misleading claims, including rankings or awards we can't check;</li>
      <li>explicit imagery, and books flagged explicit in the homepage Spotlight;</li>
      <li>links anywhere but one of the book's own store or platform pages;</li>
      <li>sweepstakes that require a purchase.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Every ad is labeled "Sponsored" and links with <code>rel="sponsored"</code>. We review each ad before it runs and may refuse
      one; a refused ad is refunded in full, automatically.
    </p>

    <h2>Prices and payment</h2>
    <p>
      Prices are in US dollars and shown before you pay. The price of a placement is fixed when its dates are generated, so a later
      price change never affects a booking. Payment is by card through Stripe, which handles your card details: we never see or
      store them. Credits and promotion codes are applied first. Your dates are held for about 30 minutes while you pay.
    </p>

    <h2>Cancellations and refunds</h2>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>When</th><th>What you get</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>We don't approve the ad</td><td>A full refund, automatically</td></tr>
        <tr><td>You cancel 7 days or more before the start</td><td>A full refund, or credit if you prefer</td></tr>
        <tr><td>You cancel 2 to 7 days before the start</td><td>Half the price as credit</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Less than 48 hours before the start</td><td>No refund: it runs as booked</td></tr>
        <tr><td>We fail to deliver (for example, a newsletter doesn't go out)</td><td>Credit for what you missed, or you can ask to rebook</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>
      Card refunds usually take 5–10 days to appear. Credits have no cash value, can't be transferred, and stay on your profile while
      it's open. Unspent Sponsored Match budget at the end of its dates becomes credit.
    </p>

    <h2>Reporting and privacy</h2>
    <p>
      You see totals: how often the ad was shown and seen, clicks, and new followers of the book. We filter out bots and email link
      scanners. We never share who saw or clicked an ad, and advertisers never receive readers' emails.
    </p>

    <h2>Author Pro</h2>
    <p>
      Author Pro renews each month or year until you cancel, which you can do at any time from Billing; it then runs to the end of
      the period you've paid for. Its promotion credit arrives once a quarter while the subscription is active. Verification and
      listing stay free whether or not you subscribe.
    </p>

    <h2>Chargebacks</h2>
    <p>
      If a payment is disputed with your bank, the profile can't buy promotions and its upcoming ones pause while we look into it.
      Please talk to us first: reply to any email from us.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>We may update these terms. Changes apply to bookings made after the date above, never to ones already paid for.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
